\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{frap}

\title{Cubies, sticker states, and fixed local frames}

\p{Use three pieces of vocabulary for the state drawn below. A
\newvocab{cubie} is one physical unit of the layered cube, with a home
position and the visible stickers incident to that position. For a
three-layer cube these are the eight corners, twelve edges, and six centres
described in [how the cube models connect](frap-001A).}

\p{A \newvocab{sticker state} assigns each labelled visible sticker to one
surface slot. In the three-layer model a slot is a pair #{(p,n)}, with #{p}
the surface-cell coordinate and #{n} its outward normal; the solved
assignment is the reference state, and a move permutes these assignments.
The correspondence between these slots, cubie fibres, and the coordinates
#{(\sigma,x;\tau,z)} is made explicit in [how the cube models connect](frap-001A).}

\p{A \newvocab{fixed local frame} specializes the
\vocabk{local frame}{frap-000Q}: it is a chosen reference ordering of the
incident sticker directions at each cubie. A move records both the cubie's
destination and how its labels are transported relative to that ordering.
The six centre directions keep the global viewing frame fixed; a whole-cube
rotation would change that frame and is a separate symmetry. These
definitions distinguish a labelled state from a colour observation, which
forgets labels that look alike.}
